== a handler for SIGUSR1, whose number differs on the two systems
  install rc=0  previous handler was default=yes
  after raise(SIGUSR1):       count=1  handler saw SIGUSR1
  after pthread_kill(SIGUSR1): count=1  handler saw SIGUSR1
== the same for SIGUSR2, which differs differently
  install rc=0  after raise(SIGUSR2): count=1  handler saw SIGUSR2
== reading the action back through oact
  query rc=0  handler is the one we installed=yes
  flags read back            SA_RESTART  stray=no
== sa_mask crosses inside the struct, not as a pointer
  install rc=0  SIGUSR2 in the mask we read back=yes  SIGINT=no
== save, replace with SIG_IGN, restore
  while ignored:   count=0  (0 is correct)
  after restore:   count=1  handler saw SIGUSR1
== back to SIG_DFL
  rc=0  oact reported our handler=yes
  now default=yes
done
